WEBVTT

00:02.690 --> 00:05.380
<i>The game was interrupted for a few minutes,</i>

00:05.380 --> 00:07.480
<i>but it is now ready to resume.</i>

00:08.070 --> 00:10.880
<i>Will Nankatsu be able to catch up?</i>

00:10.880 --> 00:12.650
<i>Will Musashi be able to hold on?</i>

00:13.460 --> 00:19.660
<i>Musashi's captain Misugi remains far in the back, leaning against the goalpost.</i>

00:19.660 --> 00:21.260
<i>Only two minutes remain!</i>

00:21.260 --> 00:24.040
<i>Which of these teams will advance to the grand finals?</i>

00:40.070 --> 00:45.680
<i>The smell of the grass when I stumbled,</i>

00:40.070 --> 00:45.680
<i>koronda toki no shibafu no nioi</i>

00:45.680 --> 00:50.730
<i>the endless blue of the sky above...</i>

00:45.680 --> 00:50.730
<i>aogimita sora no ao hateshinakatta</i>

00:51.400 --> 00:56.530
<i>This winding, back-and-forth path</i>

00:51.400 --> 00:56.530
<i>mayotte modori susumu kidô ga</i>

00:57.280 --> 01:04.870
<i>is a map for our endless dreams</i>

00:57.280 --> 01:04.870
<i>hateshinai yume o miru boku-tachi no chizu</i>

01:04.870 --> 01:10.640
<i>Even if my hopes miss the goal</i>

01:04.870 --> 01:10.640
<i>goal o soreta kibô ga atte mo</i>

01:10.640 --> 01:19.140
<i>if I stand back up, my dreams will never end</i>

01:10.640 --> 01:19.140
<i>mata tachiagaru nara yume wa owaranai</i>

01:19.140 --> 01:24.930
<i>No.1! Race forth, faster than anyone</i>

01:19.140 --> 01:24.930
<i>No. 1! dare yori hayaku kakenuke</i>

01:24.930 --> 01:30.860
<i>Make a starting dash toward the world stage with your tricky plays!</i>

01:24.930 --> 01:30.860
<i>tricky na play de sekai e muke Start! Dash!</i>

01:30.860 --> 01:32.400
<i>Run & Run!</i>

01:32.400 --> 01:39.690
<i>Aspirations are the one buzz, buzz, buzz that gets us moving</i>

01:32.400 --> 01:39.690
<i>akogare dake ga boku-ra o chiri-chiri-chiri ugokasu yo
</i>

01:39.690 --> 01:42.610
<i>Blaze, blaze, blaze! Let's go, it's kickoff!</i>

01:39.690 --> 01:42.610
<i>mera-mera-mera iku ze kickoff</i>

01:42.610 --> 01:47.540
<i>Leap out into a giant field of dreams</i>

01:42.610 --> 01:47.540
<i>tobidasô dodekai dream field</i>

01:58.380 --> 02:03.390
<b><b>EPISODE 22:
THE DESTINED ADDITIONAL TIME</b></b>

02:00.800 --> 02:02.050
Let's go, Musashi!

02:02.050 --> 02:03.680
Come, Nankatsu!

02:03.680 --> 02:07.370
<i>Nankatsu tries to open up the defense by passing the ball around.</i>

02:07.370 --> 02:10.980
<i>However, even Musashi's forwards have drawn back, and the team is fully defending!</i>

02:10.980 --> 02:15.110
<i>There's no doubt that they are trying to defend this one-goal lead.</i>

02:15.110 --> 02:18.610
Honma! Sanada! Keep marking Tsubasa like that!

02:18.610 --> 02:19.200
Eh?!

02:19.200 --> 02:22.830
At this point, Nankatsu has no one but Tsubasa to rely on.

02:22.830 --> 02:26.580
Don't think about the ball. Just focus on following Tsubasa closely!

02:26.580 --> 02:27.120
Got it!

02:27.120 --> 02:28.000
What?

02:28.000 --> 02:29.640
Come on guys, what's wrong?!

02:29.640 --> 02:32.040
They're obviously going to mark Tsubasa heavily!

02:32.740 --> 02:35.240
But Nankatsu didn't win and make it this far

02:35.240 --> 02:37.420
just on Tsubasa's strength alone!

02:37.420 --> 02:41.470
In this critical moment, it's time to use your combined strength to steal a goal from them!

02:41.470 --> 02:43.250
Wakabayashi...

02:43.250 --> 02:43.760
All right!

02:43.760 --> 02:47.100
We, the Shutetsu Trio, will break through their defense!

02:47.100 --> 02:47.640
Yes!

02:47.640 --> 02:50.140
Ichinose! Mukai! Go to the left and mark those two!

02:51.010 --> 02:51.850
What?!

02:51.850 --> 02:53.560
If this side won't work...

02:53.560 --> 02:55.560
It'll be a pass to the right!

02:55.560 --> 02:56.730
Nakajima, follow him!

02:56.730 --> 02:57.480
Yes!

02:58.480 --> 03:02.030
<i>There's nowhere for Kisugi to pass to!</i>

03:02.030 --> 03:03.280
<i>This won't do!</i>

03:03.280 --> 03:06.450
<i>Misugi is reading all of our movements.</i>

03:07.640 --> 03:10.280
<i>He's completely calm and collected.</i>

03:10.280 --> 03:13.330
<i>Thanks to Misugi's unerringly accurate direction,</i>

03:13.330 --> 03:15.420
<i>Musashi's defense is perfect.</i>

03:15.420 --> 03:17.840
<i>Good! We've got this game in the bag.</i>

03:17.840 --> 03:19.490
<i>Nankatsu is in trouble!</i>

03:19.490 --> 03:22.260
<i>They can't organize a proper attack like this at all.</i>

03:22.260 --> 03:25.340
<i>There is less than a minute remaining!</i>

03:25.340 --> 03:28.590
They are slowing down. This is our chance!

03:28.590 --> 03:30.100
Go and steal the ball.

03:30.100 --> 03:33.640
If we can take and keep the ball, we will win this match!

03:33.640 --> 03:34.560
Yes!

03:34.560 --> 03:37.840
<i>Now, Musashi is actively pressing to steal the ball!</i>

03:37.840 --> 03:41.400
<i>Keeping the ball away from Musashi is taking all Nankatsu has!</i>

03:41.400 --> 03:42.560
It's useless.

03:42.560 --> 03:44.280
We'll run out of time like this!

03:44.280 --> 03:45.640
Got it!

03:45.640 --> 03:48.660
<i>Is Nankatsu panicking?</i>

03:48.660 --> 03:51.450
<i>Musashi finally steals the ball!</i>

03:51.450 --> 03:53.040
Like hell you are!

03:53.700 --> 03:57.130
<i>Nanaktsu's Ishizaki promptly steals the ball back!</i>

03:57.130 --> 03:58.750
Nice work, Ishizaki!

03:58.750 --> 04:00.050
Let's go, everyone!

04:00.900 --> 04:03.760
<i>Nankatsu charges forward as the match nears its end!</i>

04:04.260 --> 04:09.310
<i>However, Tsubasa remains thoroughly marked.</i>

04:09.310 --> 04:10.510
Guys...

04:10.510 --> 04:11.770
It's almost over.

04:13.060 --> 04:15.390
Can't you do something about those markers?

04:15.930 --> 04:17.520
<i>Will Taki shoot?</i>

04:19.520 --> 04:21.830
<i>He doesn't! He passes the ball back.</i>

04:21.830 --> 04:23.360
<i>The pass is for Misaki.</i>

04:23.850 --> 04:25.740
<i>We can't lose yet.</i>

04:27.160 --> 04:31.910
<i>It's too early for me and my friends to play our final match together!</i>

04:31.910 --> 04:33.040
Misaki!

04:33.040 --> 04:40.000
<i>As expected, Nankatsu's second key player, Misaki, refuses to give up until the very last second!</i>

04:40.000 --> 04:44.010
Stop him! Use everything in your power to stop him!

04:44.010 --> 04:46.510
If you can, victory is as good as ours!

04:46.510 --> 04:47.920
We'll definitely stop him!

04:47.920 --> 04:49.760
We won't let him go any further!

04:49.760 --> 04:50.900
<i>Is this it...?!</i>

04:50.900 --> 04:54.640
<i>Even if the rest of them come after me, Tsubasa's markers won't budge.</i>

04:55.300 --> 04:57.520
<i>Is this really the end for us...?!</i>

04:57.520 --> 05:00.270
Misaki! Just shoot as hard as you can!

05:00.780 --> 05:01.940
<i>Wakabayashi!</i>

05:01.940 --> 05:03.260
He's right, Misaki!

05:03.260 --> 05:04.940
You can't pass it to me.

05:04.940 --> 05:06.650
Just shoot!

05:07.820 --> 05:10.830
All right! It's all or nothing!

05:10.830 --> 05:13.120
I'll cover this side, somehow!

05:13.120 --> 05:14.840
Keeper, you just jump to the right!

05:14.840 --> 05:15.450
Yes!

05:15.450 --> 05:19.000
<i>Misaki takes aim at the goal and fires away with everything he's got!</i>

05:20.800 --> 05:22.750
<i>It's blocked!</i>

05:23.260 --> 05:26.630
<i>Is this the moment that seals Musashi's victory?!</i>

05:26.630 --> 05:27.300
<i>What?!</i>

05:26.630 --> 05:29.840
<i>Not yet! The referee hasn't blown his whistle yet!</i>

05:29.840 --> 05:33.560
<i>How do you expect me to give up on this match
until the very last second?</i>

05:33.560 --> 05:34.560
Tsubasa!

05:35.560 --> 05:37.330
<i>Nankatsu has the ball again!</i>

05:37.330 --> 05:40.100
<i>Nankatsu still has one final chance!</i>

05:40.100 --> 05:44.110
Tsubasa can and will take a precise shot from such a narrow angle.

05:44.110 --> 05:46.280
Block all of his shot courses!

05:46.280 --> 05:46.860
Yes!

05:46.860 --> 05:47.780
Damn it!

05:47.780 --> 05:51.530
<i>Tsubasa won't be able to shoot!</i>

05:51.530 --> 05:56.100
<i>Surrounded as he is from all sides, Tsubasa isn't even able to send a pass!</i>

05:56.100 --> 05:57.460
<i>There's no more time!</i>

05:58.790 --> 06:01.130
Tsubasa!

06:01.130 --> 06:02.040
Tsubasa!

06:02.040 --> 06:04.420
Don't let him get that ball out of there!

06:04.420 --> 06:06.240
<i>I won't give up...!</i>

06:06.240 --> 06:08.130
<i>It's too early to call it quits!</i>

06:08.130 --> 06:10.760
<i>There must be a chance.</i>

06:10.760 --> 06:12.640
<i>Somewhere, somehow...</i>

06:12.640 --> 06:13.900
<i>I'm sure of it!</i>

06:16.930 --> 06:19.440
There's only one way out of this cage...

06:20.060 --> 06:21.580
And that way is up!

06:21.580 --> 06:22.240
What?!

06:22.240 --> 06:26.780
<i>Tsubasa kicks the ball up above his head!</i>

06:28.740 --> 06:30.450
<i>He's jumping up with the ball!</i>

06:35.870 --> 06:37.260
<i>Here it is!</i>

06:37.260 --> 06:41.710
<i>Tsubasa fires off an overhead kick in the last moments!</i>

06:41.710 --> 06:43.960
Tsu–Tsubasa!

06:44.600 --> 06:46.260
<i>That's just like you, Tsubasa.</i>

06:46.260 --> 06:48.710
<i>Showing your best, especially once you're cornered.</i>

06:48.710 --> 06:51.970
<i>But there's just no angle for this shot.</i>

06:51.970 --> 06:54.180
<i>It's too narrow.</i>

06:54.180 --> 06:56.810
<i>Musashi will win, after all!</i>

07:01.640 --> 07:02.770
All right!

07:02.770 --> 07:03.400
We did it!

07:03.400 --> 07:08.400
<i>Misaki plunges into the goal with the ball!
What a tenacious diving header!</i>

07:08.400 --> 07:09.680
<i>They are even!</i>

07:09.680 --> 07:14.490
<i>In the eleventh hour, Nankatsu manage to tie the score, 4-4!</i>

07:14.490 --> 07:17.190
I did it!

07:17.190 --> 07:18.980
<i>Misaki must be overjoyed.</i>

07:18.980 --> 07:23.360
<i>Right on the brink of defeat, he scores an invaluable goal!</i>

07:23.360 --> 07:25.900
Misaki, thank you!

07:25.900 --> 07:27.670
You really did score one for us.

07:27.670 --> 07:28.980
We did it! We did it!

07:28.980 --> 07:30.420
You did it, Misaki!

07:31.300 --> 07:32.800
Tsubasa!

07:32.800 --> 07:34.800
Tsubasa... Misaki...

07:34.800 --> 07:36.300
We have caught up!

07:36.300 --> 07:37.890
You're awesome, Misaki!

07:37.890 --> 07:39.560
Nankatsu is the best!

07:40.570 --> 07:41.600
Damn it.

07:41.600 --> 07:44.060
We were just a step away from victory!

07:44.920 --> 07:48.770
<i>So, in the end, Misaki was the real key player, here.</i>

07:48.770 --> 07:52.930
<i>And that final overhead kick Tsubasa showed us...</i>

07:52.930 --> 07:56.030
<i>It was really more of a pass than a shot.</i>

07:56.920 --> 08:00.390
<i>I made a mistake reading the game at the very end.</i>

08:00.390 --> 08:03.320
<i>I've been too naive.</i>

08:03.320 --> 08:06.080
<i>Football is hard, after all.</i>

08:06.080 --> 08:09.420
<i>There is no more time left on the clock.</i>

08:09.420 --> 08:11.430
<i>and we're now in loss time.</i>

08:11.430 --> 08:13.430
<i>The match resumes with Musashi's kick-off.</i>

08:16.970 --> 08:18.220
<i>Will it end in a tie?</i>

08:18.220 --> 08:20.470
<i>Will we go to the penalty shootout?</i>

08:20.470 --> 08:21.450
<i>Not yet!</i>

08:21.450 --> 08:24.100
<i>Don't just assume the game is over!</i>

08:24.100 --> 08:27.900
<i>Until the referee blows his whistle, until the very last second,</i>

08:27.900 --> 08:29.650
<i>I will give it my all!</i>

08:29.650 --> 08:30.900
Tsubasa...

08:30.900 --> 08:34.150
<i>Tsubasa hasn't given up on this game yet!</i>

08:34.150 --> 08:36.740
Tsubasa, you...

08:36.740 --> 08:39.490
<i>This is the last game that Misugi will ever play.</i>

08:39.490 --> 08:43.050
<i>Despite having the handicap of a heart disease,</i>

08:43.050 --> 08:45.620
<i>Misugi has challenged his limits.</i>

08:45.620 --> 08:52.130
<i>To answer Misugi's courage, I won't waste another second of this match.</i>

08:52.130 --> 08:55.130
Captain! He's going to shoot!

08:56.100 --> 08:56.940
<i>I'll stop him.</i>

08:56.940 --> 08:59.140
<i>I'll stop his shot myself!</i>

08:59.140 --> 09:00.890
Let's go, Misugi!

09:07.980 --> 09:11.440
<i>Tsubasa fires an extra long shot!</i>

09:13.050 --> 09:16.900
Go! In this damp pitch, the ball will be faster than usual!

09:16.900 --> 09:19.780
This is the nastiest kind of shot for the goalkeeper!

09:19.780 --> 09:22.330
<i>Tazawa can't reach it!</i>

09:22.330 --> 09:24.500
<i>But here comes Misugi!</i>

09:27.230 --> 09:29.750
<i>Misugi was a step too late!</i>

09:29.750 --> 09:31.750
<i>The whistle is blown at the same time!</i>

09:32.220 --> 09:33.790
<i>Which one is it?</i>

09:33.790 --> 09:37.170
<i>Is it a goal, or is it the end of the match?</i>

09:54.820 --> 09:56.900
<i>It's a goal!</i>

09:56.900 --> 09:59.110
<i>The game ends with this goal!</i>

09:59.800 --> 10:04.870
<i>The representatives of Shizuoka, Nankatsu SC, win 5-4!</i>

10:04.870 --> 10:06.690
<i>This is a miracle!</i>

10:06.690 --> 10:09.420
<i>This can't be called anything but a miraculous comeback!</i>

10:09.420 --> 10:15.050
<i>This is the fruit of Tsubasa's unwavering spirit, refusing to give up until the very end!</i>

10:16.020 --> 10:18.230
I won...

10:18.230 --> 10:19.860
Did I really just win?

10:19.860 --> 10:22.300
You did it! You did it, Tsubasa!

10:28.020 --> 10:29.570
Captain!

10:32.020 --> 10:34.130
I'm fine, manager.

10:34.940 --> 10:36.190
Misugi!

10:37.190 --> 10:39.870
Congratulations, Tsubasa.

10:39.870 --> 10:41.950
You were truly great.

10:41.950 --> 10:44.950
You won our duel.

10:44.950 --> 10:47.700
That's not true, Misugi.

10:47.700 --> 10:53.330
If you didn't have a handicap, you would have certainly stopped my final shot,

10:53.330 --> 10:56.890
and Musashi would have won this game.

10:56.890 --> 10:59.000
Thank you, Tsubasa.

10:59.000 --> 11:00.900
But it's really okay.

11:01.910 --> 11:05.350
Truly, I am satisfied, to the bottom of my heart.

11:05.350 --> 11:07.100
Misugi...

11:07.100 --> 11:10.800
I have always played only for a couple of minutes,

11:10.800 --> 11:15.860
but thanks to you being my rival,
I was finally able to play a full match.

11:15.860 --> 11:22.620
Being able to play such a great match with you until the end

11:22.620 --> 11:24.870
makes me happier than challenging you.

11:25.470 --> 11:27.870
Thank you, Tsubasa.

11:27.870 --> 11:29.870
Thank you, guys!

11:29.870 --> 11:30.900
Captain...

11:30.900 --> 11:32.370
Misugi...

11:32.370 --> 11:37.000
Sorry, Manager, but... could you lend me your shoulder,
just for a little while?

11:37.000 --> 11:43.130
Without your support, today's match wouldn't have been as good.

11:44.220 --> 11:45.640
Captain...

11:45.640 --> 11:48.440
Thank you for everything you've done until now.

11:48.440 --> 11:52.560
This will be your final task as Musashi FC's manager.

11:52.560 --> 11:54.820
Please, help me to the bench.

11:56.080 --> 11:57.550
Sure!

11:58.730 --> 12:00.190
Misugi...

12:00.190 --> 12:03.280
Dear, Jun did well.

12:03.280 --> 12:05.060
He really did well.

12:05.060 --> 12:06.700
Yes.

12:08.900 --> 12:09.950
Tsubasa!

12:10.950 --> 12:13.960
I won't stop playing football, after all.

12:16.210 --> 12:19.640
Even if I can only play for 1 or 2 minutes,

12:19.640 --> 12:22.380
I'll make sure to stand on the field.

12:22.380 --> 12:26.340
Then one day, I'll defeat this heart condition of mine.

12:26.340 --> 12:28.340
Misugi...

12:38.360 --> 12:43.090
NANKATSU SC: 5
MUSASHI FC: 4

12:56.420 --> 13:01.300
Captain, today is the day for Tsubasa's final match, isn't it?

13:01.300 --> 13:05.300
Yeah. It's a shame that I can't watch the match in Japan.

13:05.300 --> 13:07.800
We are cheering for him, too!

13:07.800 --> 13:10.550
Please, use this to watch the match once it starts.

13:10.550 --> 13:13.200
Leave the rest to us.

13:13.200 --> 13:14.910
That won't do.

13:14.910 --> 13:16.060
Oh, well...

13:16.720 --> 13:19.310
<i>Good luck, Tsubasa.</i>

13:26.940 --> 13:29.030
The old man sure is late.

13:29.030 --> 13:32.200
Really though, what is he doing?

13:33.200 --> 13:34.390
Huh?

13:36.560 --> 13:38.280
Woah, they came!

13:38.280 --> 13:39.380
True!

13:39.380 --> 13:41.880
CERTAIN VICTORY! NANKATSU

13:41.880 --> 13:43.630
It's awesome!

13:47.130 --> 13:49.260
Kept you waiting, little fellows!

13:49.260 --> 13:50.640
Hop on!

13:52.500 --> 13:55.320
Thanks for helping us come and go there every day, old man.

13:55.320 --> 13:58.140
Don't mention it! It's fine, since I'm working at the same time!

13:58.140 --> 14:00.980
Man, Nankatsu is really strong.

14:00.980 --> 14:03.400
They're worth cheering for!

14:03.400 --> 14:06.110
Tsubasa plays there; of course they would be strong!

14:06.110 --> 14:08.200
Yeah that too! Tsubasa, right?

14:08.200 --> 14:10.360
Your boyfriend, I assume!

14:10.360 --> 14:10.930
Huh?!

14:10.930 --> 14:13.490
Stop joking around, old man!

14:13.490 --> 14:16.330
Hey! Don't hit me while I'm driving!

14:16.840 --> 14:19.580
Guys, you've done a great job until now.

14:20.240 --> 14:23.920
Many things happened on the way here.

14:23.920 --> 14:26.460
Like Nishio having to leave the field due to injury.

14:26.460 --> 14:28.920
Sorry to make you worry, guys.

14:28.920 --> 14:32.140
You've done well and worked hard to fill that gap, Ishizaki.

14:33.640 --> 14:41.030
Speaking of filling the gap, Morisaki has done really well in covering for Wakabayashi.

14:41.030 --> 14:42.020
Thanks!

14:42.020 --> 14:46.180
Today, Wakabayashi will be the one protecting Nankatsu's goal.

14:46.180 --> 14:48.030
Thank you, Morisaki.

14:48.030 --> 14:50.530
I should be the one saying that, Wakabayashi.

14:50.530 --> 14:55.280
I won't let Meiwa score a single time in this goal you've protected until now!

14:56.540 --> 15:00.630
But, if Wakabayashi's leg starts acting up during the game,

15:00.630 --> 15:02.860
I will have you go in, Morisaki.

15:02.860 --> 15:05.700
Yes, sir! I've done my preparations.

15:05.700 --> 15:08.050
And Tsubasa, our captain.

15:08.050 --> 15:09.170
Yes, sir!

15:09.170 --> 15:12.890
You've done a great job leading the team this far.

15:12.890 --> 15:20.620
The rest of you, too, with no exceptions. You have done a great job!

15:20.620 --> 15:26.110
But, this is the last match you will play together.

15:26.110 --> 15:30.470
Misaki will be moving away to a new place again.

15:31.360 --> 15:37.330
And it appears that Tsubasa will be going to Brazil if we win the finals.

15:37.330 --> 15:38.700
Yeah.

15:38.700 --> 15:40.900
Listen to me, guys.

15:40.900 --> 15:46.140
You must do your absolute best in these grand finals, so you won't have any regrets.

15:46.140 --> 15:47.090
Yes, sir!

15:54.620 --> 15:59.660
<i>The National Youth Football Tournament's grand finals are here, and the teams who have made it this far</i>

15:59.660 --> 16:05.520
<i>are Saitama's representatives, Meiwa FC, and Shizuoka's representatives, Nankatsu SC.</i>

16:05.520 --> 16:08.520
<i>This year's elementary kids are so passionate!</i>

16:08.520 --> 16:13.530
<i>The stadium is already filled with people who are excited to get a good look at this match!</i>

16:23.540 --> 16:27.080
<i>Nankatsu SC's players come out to the field, first!</i>

16:27.080 --> 16:29.990
Nankatsu! Fight!

16:29.990 --> 16:30.920
Yeah!

16:30.920 --> 16:32.760
Good luck, guys!

16:32.760 --> 16:34.430
Make sure to be the champions!

16:34.430 --> 16:36.500
Oh, it's mom and the others!

16:36.500 --> 16:37.550
Dad!

16:37.550 --> 16:41.430
Hey, Ryo! I closed the bath shop to bere!

16:41.430 --> 16:44.810
Don't make any mistakes and pull others' legs!

16:44.810 --> 16:50.550
Oh, come on! If you're going to cheer,
can't you find something better to say?!

16:51.320 --> 16:53.820
<i>Dad!</i>

16:53.820 --> 16:59.330
<i>It's your last match with them.
You should do your best, Taro.</i>

16:59.330 --> 17:03.330
My dad is here! My dad!

17:07.330 --> 17:08.830
Roberto!

17:09.360 --> 17:12.340
<i>You're finally at the grand finals.</i>

17:12.340 --> 17:14.820
<i>I will win, Roberto.</i>

17:14.820 --> 17:17.640
<i>I will win, and we'll go to Brazil together!</i>

17:19.440 --> 17:22.400
<i>Nankatsu quickly get to their shooting warm-ups.</i>

17:22.400 --> 17:23.810
<i>I wonder what's wrong...</i>

17:24.500 --> 17:28.600
<i>Meiwa's players haven't arrived to the field, yet.</i>

17:28.600 --> 17:30.240
<i>They're late.</i>

17:30.240 --> 17:31.110
<i>Don't tell me...</i>

17:34.070 --> 17:37.250
<i>Because of yesterday's match, Hyuga...</i>

17:41.160 --> 17:42.740
What?!

17:47.550 --> 17:49.080
<i>They appeared!</i>

17:49.080 --> 17:51.250
<i>Meiwa FC is here!</i>

17:51.250 --> 17:55.710
<i>Finally... it's time to pay you back, Kojiro Hyuga.</i>

17:55.710 --> 17:58.930
<i>All right, Hyuga. It's on!</i>

17:58.930 --> 18:02.430
<i>Hyuga, let's win this match for sure!</i>

18:03.140 --> 18:07.440
<i>I mean, especially after everything you've said...</i>

18:08.430 --> 18:10.750
<i>Coach, how's captain's condition?</i>

18:10.750 --> 18:12.570
<i>Can he play tomorrow?</i>

18:12.570 --> 18:14.920
<i>Now now, keep it down, will ya?</i>

18:14.920 --> 18:17.980
<i>Kojiro is still not awake.</i>

18:17.980 --> 18:18.780
<i>Still?</i>

18:18.780 --> 18:21.180
<i>Then today's match is...</i>

18:21.180 --> 18:23.520
<i>Doctor, how is he?</i>

18:23.520 --> 18:28.060
<i>His fever is down, but letting him play
in a match just after waking up is...</i>

18:28.060 --> 18:30.620
<i>That's not a very funny joke, doctor.</i>

18:31.230 --> 18:32.380
<i>Captain!</i>

18:32.380 --> 18:33.670
<i>Hyuga!</i>

18:33.670 --> 18:36.630
<i>My body is back to normal.</i>

18:36.630 --> 18:39.280
<i>You all worry too much.</i>

18:39.280 --> 18:42.390
<i>Did you really think I'd just skip this match?</i>

18:42.390 --> 18:44.000
<i>Kojiro...</i>

18:44.000 --> 18:46.390
<i>Are you really all right?</i>

18:46.390 --> 18:48.610
<i>I'm fine.</i>

18:48.610 --> 18:52.150
<i>I have come this far thanks to you.</i>

18:52.150 --> 18:57.350
<i>You know, until now, I always thought
teamwork wasn't needed in football.</i>

18:57.350 --> 19:02.360
<i>But now, having stopped to think about it,
I can't play football by myself.</i>

19:04.120 --> 19:08.870
<i>We would have probably lost yesterday's match if it hadn't been for Wakashimazu.</i>

19:08.870 --> 19:13.880
<i>And we've kept winning these matches thanks to your strength, guys.</i>

19:13.880 --> 19:20.130
<i>A little teamwork is necessary,
which means believing in your teammates.</i>

19:20.130 --> 19:21.470
<i>Hyuga!</i>

19:21.470 --> 19:24.860
<i>I want to win today's match at all costs!</i>

19:24.860 --> 19:27.620
<i>Lend me your power once more, everyone!</i>

19:27.620 --> 19:29.430
<i>Okay, captain!</i>

19:29.430 --> 19:31.730
<i>I'm counting on you.</i>

19:31.810 --> 19:35.780
<i>Hyuga showed faith in his teammates for the first time.</i>

19:35.780 --> 19:37.980
<i>In order to respond to the trust he has placed in us,</i>

19:37.980 --> 19:40.990
<i>we must win this match.</i>

19:42.260 --> 19:46.990
<i>It looks like our tiger, Kojiro, was just asleep for a while.</i>

19:46.990 --> 19:53.950
<i>After just a night of rest, the tiger has come back, all grown up.</i>

19:53.950 --> 19:56.750
<i>We can do this. We can win the finals!</i>

19:59.260 --> 20:01.650
<i>I will surely win.</i>

20:06.760 --> 20:07.960
All right!

20:07.960 --> 20:10.960
Let's go to cheer big bro Kojiro!

20:10.960 --> 20:12.270
Yeah!

20:12.270 --> 20:14.460
You forgot your hat!

20:14.460 --> 20:16.400
Today will be hot.

20:16.400 --> 20:19.120
Don't forget to drink lots of liquids.

20:19.120 --> 20:20.570
All right!

20:23.320 --> 20:26.450
<i>I will finally be able to say goodbye to this kind of life.</i>

20:26.450 --> 20:30.700
<i>Let's settle our score once and for all, Nankatsu SC!</i>

20:32.710 --> 20:35.830
As we thought, those two ended up playing in the finals.

20:35.830 --> 20:37.320
Yes.

20:37.320 --> 20:42.090
<i>I will make a decision on who to scout
based on the outcome of this match.</i>

20:46.090 --> 20:48.480
All right, let's go!

20:48.480 --> 20:51.020
Meiwa's football knows no such thing as defeat!

20:51.020 --> 20:54.290
Today, we'll win as well—and we'll grasp victory!

20:54.290 --> 20:55.440
Yeah!

20:55.440 --> 20:58.570
Guys, this is our final match!

20:58.570 --> 21:01.140
Let's do our best, and play to not have any regrets!

21:01.140 --> 21:04.070
This time, we'll smash Meiwa!

21:04.070 --> 21:06.320
Yeah!

21:09.330 --> 21:12.660
Let's pour all our heart and spirit into cheering, one last time!

21:12.660 --> 21:16.960
Nankatsu! Take revenge for your first match!

21:16.960 --> 21:19.090
Go!

21:19.700 --> 21:25.420
<i>Oddly enough, this final match has the same line-ups as the first match.</i>

21:25.420 --> 21:31.430
<i>Meiwa won that time, but we can say that the two teams were equal in terms of skill.</i>

21:31.430 --> 21:39.190
<i>Not only that, but Nankatsu's usual goalkeeper, Wakabayashi, makes his comeback from injury in this match.</i>

21:39.190 --> 21:44.440
<i>Meiwa might not be able score as many goals as they did in the first match.</i>

21:44.440 --> 21:49.950
<i>However, Meiwa will be starting their mysterious goalkeeper Wakashimazu in this match,</i>

21:49.950 --> 21:54.340
<i>the one who was subbed in mid-match against Furano to stop their penalty kick.</i>

21:54.340 --> 21:58.210
<i>It looks as though they've added an extra layer to their defense.</i>

21:58.210 --> 22:00.710
<i>I'm counting on you, Wakashimazu.</i>

22:01.350 --> 22:07.720
<i>In the end, will it be Nankatsu or Meiwa standing on top of all the other teams in this country?</i>

22:08.500 --> 22:14.720
<i>The final match of the National Youth Football Tournament starts now!</i>

22:38.910 --> 22:44.800
<i>chotto are mi na ace ga tooru</i>

22:38.910 --> 22:44.800
<i>Hey, look over there at the ace passing through</i>

22:44.800 --> 22:50.800
<i>suguremono zo to machijû sawagu</i>

22:44.800 --> 22:50.800
<i>He's the best, and the whole town cheers him on</i>

22:50.800 --> 22:56.810
<i>chô-chô samba, zigzag samba</i>

22:50.800 --> 22:56.810
<i>Butterfly samba, zig-zag samba</i>

22:56.810 --> 23:02.270
<i>aitsu no uwasa de chamba mo hashiru</i>

22:56.810 --> 23:02.270
<i>Even little old ladies go around talking about him</i>

23:03.230 --> 23:08.400
<i>sore ni tsukete mo ore-tacha nan na no</i>

23:03.230 --> 23:08.400
<i>So, even if we have him, who are we?</i>

23:09.320 --> 23:15.120
<i>ball hitotsu ni kiri-kiri mai sa</i>

23:09.320 --> 23:15.120
<i>The ball spins round and round</i>

23:15.120 --> 23:21.170
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:21.170 --> 23:26.170
<i>itsuka kimeru ze inazuma shoot</i>

23:21.170 --> 23:26.170
<i>One day, I'll score with a lightning shot!</i>

23:27.460 --> 23:33.340
<i>son toki ore ga super hero sa</i>

23:27.460 --> 23:33.340
<i>When that happens, I'll become a super hero!</i>

23:33.340 --> 23:39.230
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:39.230 --> 23:46.110
<i>moete seishun kakenukero</i>

23:39.230 --> 23:46.110
<i>This fierce youth is on the field!</i>

23:50.200 --> 24:00.810
COMING UP, EPISODE 23:
PRODIGY KEEPER RETURNS!
